# Environment configuration template — copy to .env and fill in real values.
# Never commit .env. See docs/architecture/technical-architecture.md §23 for
# the full configuration-category rationale.

NODE_ENV=development

# --- Deployment tier (Phase 13) ---
# development | staging | production. Deliberately separate from NODE_ENV
# (which Next.js always sets to "production" for any optimized build,
# including a Vercel preview/staging deployment) and from Vercel's own
# VERCEL_ENV (which won't exist on the eventual self-hosted/DigitalOcean
# deployment). Drives environment-aware SEO behavior (robots.ts/
# sitemap.ts force noindex/empty unless this is "production") and will
# gate any future real analytics/notification destination the same way.
# Set explicitly per deployment — never left to default in a real
# deployment, since the default ("development") is the intentionally
# cautious fallback if this is forgotten.
APP_ENV=development

# --- Database (required — src/lib/db.ts) ---
# Local dev default matches docker-compose.yml's postgres service.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://jawaher:jawaher_dev_password@localhost:5432/jawaher_dev?schema=public"

# --- Public site origin (sitemap.xml, robots.txt, canonical/OG URLs) ---
# Real production domain is an open decision — leave unset locally (falls
# back to http://localhost:3000) and set this to the real domain once chosen.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=https://example.com

# --- Internal/scheduler-only endpoints (Phase 4, extended Phase 12/13) ---
# Required in production for /api/v1/internal/* (the inventory-reservation
# sweep, and Phase 12's ERP-push retry sweep) to accept any request at all
# — optional locally.
# INTERNAL_API_SECRET=
#
# Vercel Cron specifically (Phase 13, staging-only for now — see
# vercel.json and docs/architecture/production-readiness.md's Phase 13
# section): Vercel automatically attaches "Authorization: Bearer
# $CRON_SECRET" to a cron-triggered request. Set this to the SAME value
# as INTERNAL_API_SECRET above (one real secret, two env-var names — the
# second name is fixed by Vercel's own convention, not a design choice)
# so a Vercel Cron trigger authenticates the same way any other scheduler
# already does. Irrelevant outside Vercel.
# CRON_SECRET=

# --- Inventory reservation TTL (Phase 4) ---
# How long a soft inventory hold survives (minutes) — NOT a finalized
# business rule, see docs/planning/commerce-completeness-audit.md §5.
# Defaults to 15 if unset.
# INVENTORY_RESERVATION_TTL_MINUTES=15

# --- ERP Adapter (Phase 8 — integration foundation) ---
# Server-only. Never prefixed NEXT_PUBLIC_, never committed with a real
# value. Get all three by running, in the ERP repo:
#   npm run provision:website-integration
# which prints them once (the API key cannot be retrieved again after).
# ERP_BASE_URL=http://localhost:3000
# ERP_API_KEY=
# ERP_CONNECTION_ID=
# ERP_REQUEST_TIMEOUT_MS=5000

# --- Reserved for later phases (leave unset until the corresponding phase) ---
# (No session-signing secret: src/lib/session.ts uses an opaque,
# database-looked-up session id, deliberately never a signed/stateless
# token — there is nothing for a secret to sign. See src/lib/env.ts's
# comment if this project ever reconsiders that.)

# OTP provider (Backend phase — provider itself is an open business decision)
# OTP_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Payment Adapter (Commerce phase — gateway is an open business decision)
# PAYMENT_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Shipping Adapter (Commerce phase — courier is an open business decision)
# SHIPPING_PROVIDER_API_KEY=

# Analytics (Analytics phase — GA4 assumed, not confirmed)
# ANALYTICS_GA4_ID=

# Object storage / CDN (Media phase)
# STORAGE_BUCKET_URL=
